\f0\b \cf0 Session hijacking
\f1\b0  \'97 confirmed on commercial cores\cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 OAI-CN-5G UPF, PFCP / N4
\f1\b0  \'97 a Session Modification Request creates a 
\f0\b duplicate PDR
\f1\b0  with Precedence 10 alongside the legitimate uplink PDR at Precedence 100. Lower precedence matches first, so the UPF silently forwards the victim's uplink traffic to an attacker-controlled FAR. No validation or rejection of the conflicting PDR. 
\f0\b Reproduced on two commercial 5G cores under default configuration
\f1\b0 , one in a partner vendor lab with sanction. The paper's headline result.\cell 
